---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="JSONL Inspector — validate JSON Lines locally" description="Validate UTF-8 JSONL files up to 1 MiB, find malformed records with line numbers, preview the normalized output and download locally. No upload required.">
 <div class="tool-intro"><span class="eyebrow"><span class="pulse"></span> 01 / BROWSER WORKSPACE · NO UPLOAD</span><h1>JSONL Inspector</h1><p>Turn JSON Lines into validated, normalized records. Errors point to the first invalid line. Everything runs in your browser with no server upload.</p><div class="proof-strip"><span>JSON objects only</span><span>1 MiB max</span><span>5,000 records</span><span>Download .jsonl</span></div></div>
 <noscript><p class="notice warn">This data-processing utility requires JavaScript. Your files are never submitted to a server; enable JavaScript to validate JSONL locally.</p></noscript>
 <div class="workspace">
  <section class="panel" aria-labelledby="input-title">
   <div class="panel-title"><div><span class="kicker">INPUT / 01</span><h2 id="input-title">Source records</h2></div><span class="ordinal">01</span></div>
   <form id="jsonl-form">
    <div class="field"><label for="jsonl-file">Choose a JSONL file (UTF-8, up to 1 MiB)</label><input id="jsonl-file" type="file" accept=".jsonl,.ndjson,.txt,application/x-ndjson,text/plain"/><p class="hint">Selecting a file clears pasted data. No data is uploaded.</p></div>
    <div class="separator"><span>OR PASTE TEXT</span></div>
    <div class="field"><div class="label-row"><label for="jsonl-paste">Or paste JSON Lines</label><button id="sample" class="text-link" type="button">Load sample</button></div><textarea id="jsonl-paste" rows="9" spellcheck="false" autocapitalize="off" placeholder={'{"id":1,"name":"Asha"}\n{"id":2,"name":"Lee"}'}></textarea><p class="hint">One JSON object per line. No arrays, primitives or JSON5 comments.</p></div>
    <div class="option-row"><label for="allow-blank">Ignore empty lines</label><input id="allow-blank" type="checkbox"/></div>
    <div class="actions"><button class="button button-primary" id="process" type="submit">Validate JSONL <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></button><button class="button button-secondary" id="reset" type="button">Reset</button><button class="button button-secondary" id="cancel" type="button" hidden>Cancel</button></div>
    <p id="status" role="status" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true">Ready for input.</p>
   </form>
  </section>
  <section class="panel results-panel" aria-labelledby="output-title">
   <div class="panel-title"><div><span class="kicker">OUTPUT / 02</span><h2 id="output-title">Inspection</h2></div><span class="ordinal">02</span></div>
   <div id="empty"><div class="placeholder" aria-hidden="true"><span>{'{}'}</span></div><h3>Your result appears here.</h3><p>Provide a file or paste JSONL, then run validation. The preview and download are based on real parsed data.</p><span class="footnote">NO DATA LEAVES YOUR DEVICE</span></div>
   <div id="result" hidden>
    <div class="success-banner"><span aria-hidden="true">✓</span><div><strong>Validation complete</strong><small>Normalized output is ready.</small></div></div>
    <div class="metrics"><div><small>RECORDS</small><strong id="records">0</strong></div><div><small>BLANK LINES</small><strong id="skipped">0</strong></div><div><small>OUTPUT BYTES</small><strong id="bytes">0</strong></div></div>
    <h3 class="preview-title">Record preview <span>First 8</span></h3><ol id="preview" class="preview-list" aria-label="Parsed records"></ol>
    <a id="download" hidden class="button button-primary download" download="normalized.jsonl">Download normalized JSONL <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
    <p class="hint">Output uses one compact JSON object per line. Object-property order may be normalized by JSON serialization. Validate before replacing original data.</p>
   </div>
  </section>
 </div>
 <section class="section explanation"><div class="section-head"><div><span class="kicker">02 / REFERENCE</span><h2>How validation works</h2></div></div><div class="three-grid"><article><span class="number">01</span><h3>Decode the file</h3><p>Selected files are read as UTF-8. Invalid byte sequences fail rather than being silently replaced.</p></article><article><span class="number">02</span><h3>Validate each line</h3><p>Each non-empty line must contain a JSON object. Broken syntax and unsupported primitives are rejected with a line number.</p></article><article><span class="number">03</span><h3>Export the result</h3><p>Each accepted object is JSON-stringified and written as one line. The preview is text only, never executable HTML.</p></article></div></section>
 <section class="notice">This is a bounded local technical demonstration. It does not validate a schema, detect duplicate JSON object keys, preserve original whitespace, support JSON5 or guarantee compatibility with all JSONL consumers. The example-domain canonical is a placeholder; this starter is NOT publicly deployed.</section>
 <script is:inline type="module" src="/scripts/jsonl-ui.mjs"></script>
</Base>
